      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Dallas–Fort Worth homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Local figures from a Dallas operator and the Angi, Thumbtack and Care.com city pages, plus a national figure labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Deep clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$220–$440</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, 2,200 sq ft home, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>$550 (about $0.25 per sq ft)</td></tr><tr><td>Four-hour deep clean, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>About $200</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$140–$280</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$350–$600+</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly rate, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>About $50, range $25–$75</td></tr><tr><td>Top pros, Dallas (Thumbtack)</td><td>$75–$140</td></tr><tr><td>Listed cleaner, Dallas (Care.com)</td><td>$21.61/hr average</td></tr><tr><td>Listed cleaner, Fort Worth (Care.com)</td><td>$19.89/hr average</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, national average (Angi, national)</td><td>$260 — most pay $180–$375</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. The $21.61 Care.com figure is one listed individual. The $50 Angi figure is a company rate, and a company often sends two cleaners — more per hour, done sooner. Compare the finished price and the checklist, not the hourly number.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Dallas–Fort Worth?</h3><p><strong>Size, first.</strong> Angi prices Dallas by the square foot: deep cleaning about $0.25 per square foot against $0.10–$0.20 for a standard clean. The median Dallas home is about 2,200 sq ft, which is how you get to $550. A 1,200 sq ft Arlington apartment is a different job entirely.</p><p><strong>Texas dust and new construction.</strong> Dallas Maids flags it plainly: dust gets into Dallas homes even with the windows closed, and new construction runs from Frisco down through Dallas. Dust settles on blinds, baseboards and ceiling fans — exactly what a deep clean is priced to clear.</p><p><strong>Tile, grout and muggy summers.</strong> Tile floors are common in Dallas–Fort Worth kitchens and bathrooms, and grout scrubbing is slow work. Thumbtack\'s Dallas guidance adds that muggy summers can bring bathroom mold — slower to deal with in older Lake Highlands (75243) homes than in a new build.</p><p><strong>How long since the last deep clean.</strong> A first visit is priced like a reset, because it is one. Grease and buildup take time the first time through. After that, the home holds with standard visits at $140–$280.</p><h3>Deep clean or standard clean — what does the extra money buy?</h3><p>A standard clean covers the regular rooms: kitchen surfaces, bathrooms, floors, dusting. A deep clean adds the buildup — baseboards, grout, ceiling fans, blinds and window tracks, and behind and under furniture and appliances.</p><p>That gap is the $140–$280 standard range against $220–$440 for deep on Dallas Maids\' list. If your home gets a regular clean already, you probably do not need the deep price. If nobody has touched the baseboards or grout in a year, a standard clean will not catch you up.</p><p>Inside the oven, fridge and cabinets are add-ons with many companies. Name them before the visit, in writing, or expect them to be extra.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get a real deep clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Book the deep clean once, then maintain it.</strong> Pay the deep price for the reset, then drop to standard visits — no reset prices twice a year.</li><li><strong>Clear the clutter before they arrive.</strong> Time spent moving toys and mail is time not spent on grout.</li><li><strong>Point the visit at kitchens and bathrooms.</strong> That is where the buildup lives. Bedrooms can stay standard if money is tight.</li><li><strong>Book ahead of the rush.</strong> Thumbtack notes spring cleaning season and the weeks before major holidays get packed in Dallas — booking early gets you the slot and sometimes a better price.</li></ul><h3>A Dallas–Fort Worth deep cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Love My Maids</strong> is a deep cleaning business listed on Van Squads, offering deep cleaning at your location in ZIP 76013 in Arlington. See its listing and request a quote: <a href="/business/love-my-maids">Love My Maids on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 10 deep cleaning businesses in the metro, in two clusters — five cover Lake Highlands, Dallas ZIP 75243, and five cover Arlington ZIP 76013: <a href="/#/browse?zip=76013">search deep cleaning near 76013</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/deep-cleaning/dallas-fort-worth/\">Deep cleaning in Dallas–Fort Worth</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>In Dallas? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75243">search deep cleaning near 75243</a>.</p><p>Keeping the home up after the reset? See the Dallas–Fort Worth house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-dallas-fort-worth/">How much does house cleaning cost in Dallas–Fort Worth?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Dallas Maids — How Much Does House Cleaning Cost in Dallas? (2026 Pricing Guide) (standard cleaning $140–$280, deep cleaning $220–$440, move-out cleaning $350–$600 or more, apartment cleaning $120–$240; most professional companies charge a flat rate averaging around $50 per hour per cleaner; Dallas dust gets in even with windows closed and new construction runs from Frisco to Dallas) (dallasmaids.com); Angi — How Much Does Professional House Cleaning Cost in Dallas, TX? (Dallas average $163 per visit; hourly average about $50, range $25–$75; a deep cleaning that requires four hours would cost about $200; standard clean $0.10–$0.20 per sq ft; deep clean about $0.25 per sq ft and $550 at the median 2,200 sq ft home; move-out about $0.35 per sq ft and $770 at 2,200 sq ft; tile floors common in Dallas kitchens, bathrooms and laundry rooms — updated Oct 24, 2025) (angi.com); Thumbtack — The Best Deep House Cleaning Services in Dallas, TX (the best house cleaners in Dallas charge between $75 and $140; price depends on bedrooms, bathrooms, the state of the home and the type of service; window, fridge and oven cleaning may add to the cost) (thumbtack.com); Thumbtack — 2026 House Cleaning Prices in Dallas (hiring a pro in Dallas typically $181–$322; a deep clean for a large home may reach $484; spring cleaning season and the weeks before major holidays are usually packed — book early) (thumbtack.com); Care.com — House Cleaning Services in Dallas, TX (average cost of hiring a house cleaner in Dallas around $21.61 per hour as of October 2026) (care.com); Care.com — House Cleaning Services in Fort Worth, TX (average cost of hiring a house cleaner in Fort Worth around $19.89 per hour as of October 2026) (care.com); Angi — How Much Does It Cost to Deep Clean a House? [2026 Data], updated Sep 29, 2026 (national average $260, most homeowners pay $180–$375 — national figures, labeled national) (angi.com).</div>'
