      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Omaha homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Omaha and Nebraska sources:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical Omaha price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cleaner by the hour, Omaha (Care.com, Oct 2026)</td><td>$20.54/hr starting, up to $25.20/hr</td></tr><tr><td>Company cleaner by the hour, Omaha (MaidProfit)</td><td>$24–$40 per cleaner</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, Omaha (MaidProfit)</td><td>$110–$235 per visit</td></tr><tr><td>Every-other-week clean, Omaha (Pink Shoe)</td><td>$145–$300+ per visit</td></tr><tr><td>Omaha average, cleaning services (HomeAdvisor, cited by Pink Shoe)</td><td>$172 per visit</td></tr><tr><td>Flat-rate standard clean, Omaha (Adalyn\'s)</td><td>Studio from $119; each bedroom adds $10</td></tr><tr><td>Deep cleaning, Nebraska (MaidProfit, state figures)</td><td>$215–$425</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out cleaning, Nebraska (MaidProfit, state figures)</td><td>$245–$465</td></tr><tr><td>House cleaning, national (Thumbtack, labeled national)</td><td>$25–$50/hr per cleaner</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The hourly gap trips people up. Care.com\'s $20.54 is a starting rate for cleaners listed there, often one person you hire direct. Company crews in Omaha run $24 to $40 an hour per cleaner (MaidProfit). A direct hire may not include insurance, bonding, or a backup cleaner on a sick day (Pink Shoe). Compare the whole deal, not just the hourly number.</p><p>This is where people overpay: paying a deep-clean price for a home that only needs a standard visit, or booking one-time cleans again and again. Weekly service usually brings the per-visit rate down by roughly 10% against every-other-week (Pink Shoe). One Omaha company takes 20% off weekly visits from the second clean onward (Adalyn\'s).</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Omaha?</h3><p><strong>Home size and bathrooms.</strong> Bathrooms take the most detail work per square foot, so they move the quote fast (Pink Shoe). Adalyn\'s builds its Omaha flat rate from bedrooms first — a studio starts at $119 and each bedroom adds $10 — with bathrooms priced on top.</p><p><strong>The basement.</strong> Nebraska homes often have basements, and a finished basement adds real cleaning area (MaidProfit). A ranch in Northwest Omaha (68116, 68134) with a finished lower level is a bigger job than the square footage upstairs suggests. Say whether the basement is in or out before you book.</p><p><strong>Which side of the metro you are on.</strong> Care.com puts Omaha starting pay at $20.54 an hour, but Elkhorn starts at $22.44 and Papillion at $23.62, while Bellevue starts lower, at $19.16. A quote in Elkhorn or Papillion that sits above a central Omaha quote is following the local rates, not padding.</p><p><strong>First clean vs. recurring.</strong> A first visit can take about three times as long as a normal one while the home is brought up to a maintenance level (Pink Shoe). After that, a two-person crew usually finishes a top-to-bottom clean in one to three hours.</p><p><strong>Pets and buildup.</strong> Pet hair adds vacuuming time, and a home that has gone months without a clean takes longer than one on a schedule (Pink Shoe; MaidProfit). Name both up front and the quote holds.</p><h3>How to pay less without getting a worse clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Pick a schedule and keep it.</strong> Weekly visits cost about 10% less per visit than every-other-week ones in Omaha (Pink Shoe). Skipping months and booking catch-up cleans costs more in the end.</li><li><strong>Get a flat price in writing.</strong> Bedrooms, bathrooms and square footage are enough for a flat quote. An open hourly quote on a big West Omaha home can drift.</li><li><strong>Pick up clutter before the crew arrives.</strong> Cleaners work around piles instead of moving them, and that slows the visit (Pink Shoe). Your money should buy cleaning time, not tidying time.</li><li><strong>Near Offutt? Plan move-out cleans early.</strong> The base by Bellevue keeps relocation cleaning in steady demand around the south metro (MaidProfit). Book the empty-home clean before your move date is locked, not after.</li></ul><h3>An Omaha house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Majestic Cleaning Omaha</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location in Omaha ZIP 68114. See its listing: <a href="/business/majestic-cleaning-omaha">Majestic Cleaning Omaha on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 19 house cleaning businesses in the Omaha metro — seven in ZIP 68114, seven in Northwest Omaha ZIP 68116, three in Northwest Omaha ZIP 68134, and two in Bellevue ZIP 68005: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68114">search house cleaning near 68114</a>.</p><p>In Northwest Omaha? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68116">search house cleaning near 68116</a>.</p><p>In Bellevue? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68005">search house cleaning near 68005</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/house-cleaning/omaha/">House cleaning in Omaha</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Care.com — How much does house cleaning cost in Omaha, NE? (Oct 2026: Omaha starting $20.54/hr, max $25.20/hr; Nebraska starting $20.28/hr, max $24.81/hr; national starting $21.62/hr, max $26.28/hr; nearby starting rates: Bellevue $19.16/hr, Elkhorn $22.44/hr, Papillion $23.62/hr, Council Bluffs $21.18/hr) (care.com); Pink Shoe Cleaning Crew — House Cleaning Cost in Omaha, NE: 2026 Price Guide (every-other-week visits $145–$300+; weekly about 10% less per visit; HomeAdvisor Omaha average $172 cited on the page; Thumbtack national average $25–$50/hr per cleaner cited on the page; two-person crew finishes a top-to-bottom clean in 1–3 hours; first visit can take about three times a normal visit; bathrooms take the most detail work per square foot; clutter slows the crew; a direct hire may not include insurance, bonding or a replacement cleaner) (pinkshoecleaningcrew.com); MaidProfit — How Much Do Cleaning Services Cost in Nebraska? (Omaha: $24–$40/hr per cleaner, standard home cleaning $110–$235; Nebraska: standard $100–$225, deep $215–$425, move-out $245–$465; Nebraska homes often have basements that add significant cleaning area; Offutt Air Force Base near Bellevue drives military relocation cleaning needs; pet hair and dander add work) (maidprofit.com); Adalyn\'s Cleaning — Free Cleaning Quote, Omaha NE (flat rate quoted up front; studio starts at $119 and each bedroom adds $10; under 1,000 sq ft adds nothing; recurring discounts from the second clean onward: weekly 20% off, bi-weekly 15%, monthly 10%; bathrooms priced separately as the most labor-intensive rooms) (adalynscleaning.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-10-31 via Supabase: 19 active House cleaning businesses serve the Omaha metro ZIPs — 68114 (7), 68116 (7), 68134 (3), 68005 Bellevue (2); featured business Majestic Cleaning Omaha, House cleaning, ZIP 68114, logo on file. Every Omaha listing in this category carries a single service ZIP.</div>'
