      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Omaha drivers actually pay</h3><p>Published prices from Omaha mobile detailers:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exterior detail, sedan (Prima)</td><td>$99</td></tr><tr><td>Exterior detail, sedan / SUV / truck-van (Flawless)</td><td>$125 / $159 / $189</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail, sedan (Prima / Flawless)</td><td>$170 / $175</td></tr><tr><td>Full bundle, sedan (K3)</td><td>$200</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail, sedan / SUV / truck / 3-row SUV (Prima)</td><td>$275 / $315 / $325 / $355</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail, sedan / SUV / truck-van (Flawless)</td><td>$275 / $339 / $399</td></tr><tr><td>Premium Plus detail, free pickup and delivery (Hometown)</td><td>$359.99</td></tr><tr><td>Ceramic coating (Flawless, 1-year / 5-year)</td><td>$449 / $1,099</td></tr><tr><td>Add-ons (Flawless): heavy pet hair / engine bay</td><td>$45 / $69</td></tr><tr><td>Add-ons (Prima): pet hair / clay bar + sealant / headlight pair</td><td>from $100 / $100 / $130</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile detailing, national (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$144–$254 average, $95 low to $390 high</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Read the package, not the headline. K3\'s $200 sedan bundle and ANKA\'s $499 complete appointment are both "full details" on paper. They are not the same hours of work.</p><p>This is where people overpay: ceramic and flagship money on a daily driver. Invictus puts its Diamond Detail at $1,500–$2,400, and Prima\'s paint correction runs to $1,550 for a sedan. On the family SUV that eats crackers in the back seat, a $275–$399 full detail does the job.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Omaha?</h3><p><strong>Vehicle size, every time.</strong> Prima steps a full detail from $275 for a sedan to $355 for a 3-row SUV. Flawless steps it from $275 to $399 for a truck or van. More rows, more glass, more carpet — more time.</p><p><strong>Pet hair is priced all over the map here.</strong> Flawless charges $45 for heavy pet hair removal. Prima starts at $100 and goes up with severity, assessed on arrival. Hometown charges $139.99. Same dog, three prices. Send a photo of the back seat before you book and get the number in writing.</p><p><strong>November means salt season is coming.</strong> Omaha winters drop road salt and brine on everything. ANKA runs a Salt &amp; Brine Reset from $289, a 2–3 hour winter recovery detail. Flawless built its exterior pitch around pulling road salt and bug splatter off the paint — the bug part is the I-80 summer drive, the salt part starts now. A detail before the first brine trucks roll is cheaper than correction work in March.</p><p><strong>Cold changes how mobile works.</strong> Prima\'s rule: below 32°F, service defaults to drop-off unless you can provide a heated garage. At 32°F or higher, mobile runs as usual. A January booking may not happen in your driveway at all.</p><p><strong>Water and power — ask who brings them.</strong> Prima and Invictus both run self-contained units, with their own water and power. K3 says the opposite: it has to use your power and water, and mobile is free within 25 miles of Omaha, then $1 a mile. In a downtown (68102) apartment lot with no spigot, that decides who can take the job.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse detail</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Buy the half you need.</strong> If the paint is fine and the cabin is the problem, interior-only runs $170–$175 for a sedan.</li><li><strong>Use maintenance pricing.</strong> Prima\'s monthly plan starts at $175 a month, and its bi-weekly sedan detail is $85. A car on a plan never needs the big rescue detail.</li><li><strong>Name the mess up front.</strong> Pet hair, stains, and odor are add-ons on every Omaha list — $35 for stain extraction and $59 for odor treatment at Flawless. Priced before the visit, they\'re line items. Found during it, they\'re a renegotiation.</li><li><strong>Get the total before work starts.</strong> Flawless lists upfront pricing and Invictus posts its rates before you book. If a quote can\'t be written down, keep looking.</li></ul><h3>An Omaha mobile detailing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Flawless Mobile Car Detailing Omaha</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering mobile auto detailing at your location in Omaha ZIPs 68132, 68102, and 68108. See its listing: <a href="/business/flawless-mobile-car-detailing-omaha">Flawless Mobile Car Detailing Omaha on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 8 mobile auto detailing businesses in the Omaha metro: five listings cover each of ZIPs 68132, 68102, and 68108, plus three in ZIP 68154: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68132">search mobile auto detailing near 68132</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/mobile-auto-detailing/omaha/">Mobile auto detailing in Omaha</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>House needs work too? See the Omaha handyman cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-a-handyman-cost-in-omaha/">How much does a handyman cost in Omaha?</a> and the Omaha house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-omaha/">How much does house cleaning cost in Omaha?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Flawless Mobile Car Detailing Omaha — Mobile Car Detailing in Omaha, NE (published price list: exterior sedan $125 / SUV $159 / truck-van $189; interior sedan $175 / SUV $215 / truck-van $249; full detail sedan $275 / SUV $339 / truck-van $399; ceramic coating 1-year $449, 3-year $749, 5-year $1,099; add-ons: engine bay clean $69, heavy pet hair removal $45, odor treatment $59, stain extraction $35; exterior detail about an hour, interior or full detail 2 to 3 hours; based in Omaha, NE 68108, serving about 25 miles of downtown) (flawlessdetailing.site); Prima Mobile Detailing — Mobile Detailing FAQ, Omaha (Full Detail sedan $275 / SUV $315 / truck $325 / 3-row SUV $355; Interior Detail sedan $170 / SUV $201 / truck $230 / 3-row SUV $285; Exterior Detail sedan $99 / SUV $119 / truck $129 / 3-row SUV $149; add-ons: pet hair removal from $100, seat shampoo + extraction $75, carpet shampoo + extraction $75, clay bar + sealant $100, headlight restoration $130; monthly maintenance sedan $175, bi-weekly sedan $85; full detail 3–5 hours; fully mobile and self-contained with own water and power; below 32°F services default to drop-off unless a heated garage is available) (primadetailing.com); Invictus Mobile Auto Care &amp; Detail Studio — Omaha (interior packages $225 to $400, interior-and-exterior packages $325 to $550, flagship Diamond Detail $1,500 to $2,400, every price posted before booking; mobile unit carries its own water tank and generator) (invictusmobileautocare.com); K3 Auto Detailing — Omaha (sedan Full Bundle $200 in its booking estimator; mobile free within 25 miles of Omaha, $1/mile after that; uses your power and water) (k3autodetailing.com); ANKA Executive Detailing — Omaha (complete interior-and-exterior appointment $499, 4–6 hours; Salt &amp; Brine Reset from $289, about 2–3 hours; address 1501 Mike Fahey Street, Omaha, NE 68102) (ankaexecutivedetailing.com); Hometown Detailing — Omaha (Premium Plus Detail Package $359.99, 4–6 hours, free pickup and delivery; pet hair removal $139.99) (hometowndetailing.com); Thumbtack — 2026 Mobile Car Detailing Prices (national average $144–$254, low-end $95, high-end $390 — national figures, labeled national) (thumbtack.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-01 via Supabase: 8 active Mobile auto detailing businesses serve the Omaha metro ZIPs — 68132 (5 listings), 68102 (5), 68108 (5), 68154 (3); businesses covering several ZIPs count in each, distinct total is 8; featured business Flawless Mobile Car Detailing Omaha, Mobile auto detailing, ZIPs 68132, 68102, and 68108, logo on file.</div>'
