      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Omaha homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Omaha pages, plus national rows labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>House washing, up to 2,500 sq ft, Omaha (Window Genie of Omaha)</td><td>$225</td></tr><tr><td>Flat surface cleaning, up to 2,500 sq ft, Omaha (Window Genie of Omaha)</td><td>$225</td></tr><tr><td>Roof washing, up to 3,000 sq ft, Omaha (Window Genie of Omaha)</td><td>$299</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, Omaha (Brush &amp; Roll Painting)</td><td>$250–$500</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, Omaha (No Pressure Power Washing)</td><td>$250–$600</td></tr><tr><td>Pressure washing, per sq ft of property size (Thumbtack, Omaha page)</td><td>$0.10–$0.17</td></tr><tr><td>House / siding wash (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$170–$360</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$100–$260</td></tr><tr><td>Deck or patio (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$200–$240</td></tr><tr><td>Fence (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$180–$300</td></tr><tr><td>Roof (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$250–$600</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $225 quote and a $500 quote can both be honest. One is a flat price with a size cap — up to 2,500 sq ft. The other may be a bigger house, a second story, or heavier buildup. Ask whether your house fits under the cap before you compare totals.</p><p>The per-square-foot math needs care too. Thumbtack\'s Omaha figure is per square foot of your property size — a quote priced per square foot of the surface itself is a different number, even at the same rate.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Omaha?</h3><p><strong>Winter salt is the big one.</strong> Concrete drives, walks, and patios in Omaha collect salt residue all winter, then spring pollen, then summer mildew (That 1 Painter, Omaha–Council Bluffs). A driveway washed every spring is a short job. One that sat through two winters of salt needs pre-treatment and a second pass.</p><p><strong>Humid summers grow a green film.</strong> Omaha summers are humid, and mildew and algae build up on shaded sides of a house — a green film on siding, black streaks on a roof (No Pressure Power Washing). That growth is soft wash work: solution and dwell time, not just water.</p><p><strong>Old brick doesn\'t take a hard blast.</strong> Omaha\'s historic brick homes in Dundee need pressure matched to the masonry so aged mortar isn\'t harmed (That 1 Painter). The same crew soft-washes stucco two-stories in Bemis Park and aluminum-sided ranches in Ralston and Millard, and saves high pressure for concrete.</p><p><strong>Bigger house, bigger bill.</strong> Brush &amp; Roll puts Omaha house washing at $250–$500 depending on home size, surface material, and how much cleaning the exterior needs. A two-story house in Midtown (68105) with tight side yards costs more than a one-story ranch with open access.</p><h3>Should your house be pressure washed or soft washed?</h3><p>Concrete driveways and walkways get high pressure. Painted siding and stucco get a soft wash — lower pressure with cleaning solution (That 1 Painter, Omaha–Council Bluffs).</p><p>Hot water is the other upsell to check. HomeGuide puts plain pressure washing at $0.08–$0.20 per sq ft nationally, and power washing — heated water — at $0.35–$0.77 nationally. Hot water earns its price on greasy concrete. On plain salt film and pollen, it usually doesn\'t.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get it clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Bundle surfaces in one visit.</strong> Window Genie of Omaha advertises 10% multi-service discounts on its Omaha price page. House, driveway, and walkway in one stop beats three separate trips.</li><li><strong>Wash in spring, after salt season.</strong> The salt is already on the concrete by March. One spring wash clears the whole winter. A fall wash just gets salted over again.</li><li><strong>Price the rental honestly.</strong> Renting a power washer in Omaha runs about $40–$80 a day (Brush &amp; Roll). Cheap for a driveway. A bad trade on siding — the wrong pressure etches concrete, strips paint, and can force water behind siding.</li><li><strong>Get the cap in writing.</strong> If a quote says "up to 2,500 sq ft," ask what your house measures and what the price becomes if it\'s over.</li></ul><h3>An Omaha pressure washing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Big Red Power Washing</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering pressure washing at your location in Omaha ZIP 68105 (Midtown Omaha). See its listing: <a href="/business/big-red-power-washing">Big Red Power Washing on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 6 pressure washing businesses in the Omaha metro, all covering ZIP 68105: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68105">search pressure washing near 68105</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/pressure-washing/omaha/">Pressure washing in Omaha</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>House needs work inside too? See the Omaha house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-omaha/">How much does house cleaning cost in Omaha?</a>, the Omaha handyman cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-a-handyman-cost-in-omaha/">How much does a handyman cost in Omaha?</a>, the Omaha mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-omaha/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Omaha?</a> and the Omaha deep cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-deep-cleaning-cost-in-omaha/">How much does deep cleaning cost in Omaha?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Window Genie of Omaha — Omaha Services Pricing (house washing $225 up to 2,500 sq ft; flat surface cleaning $225 up to 2,500 sq ft; roof washing $299 up to 3,000 sq ft; 10% multi-service discounts noted on the page) (windowgenie.com); Brush &amp; Roll Painting — How Much Does It Cost To Power Wash Your House in Omaha, NE? (house wash typically $250–$500 depending on home size, surface material, and extent of cleaning required; renting a power washer for one day in Omaha is about $40–$80) (blog.brushandrollpainting.com); No Pressure Power Washing — Blog for Omaha (house wash $250–$600 varying by size and condition; standard cleaning for a small home\'s exterior $250–$400, deep cleaning $450 or more; humid Omaha summers drive mildew and algae on shaded siding and black streaks on roofs; winter salt and grime reach siding, concrete driveways, and brick in the Omaha area) (pressurewashingomaha.com); Thumbtack — The 10 Best Pressure Washing Services in Omaha, NE (pressure washing about $0.10–$0.17 per square foot of your property size; pressure washing a house at least once a year; a house wash takes from 30 minutes to several hours) (thumbtack.com); That 1 Painter Omaha - Council Bluffs — Pressure Washing in Omaha - Council Bluffs (soft wash for painted siding and stucco, high pressure for concrete driveways and walkways; concrete drives, walks, and patios collect winter salt residue, spring pollen, and summer mildew across Omaha, Elkhorn, and Council Bluffs; historic brick homes need pressure matched to the masonry in Dundee and Council Bluffs; soft-wash chemistry on stucco Bemis Park two-stories and aluminum Ralston and Millard ranches) (that1painter.com); HomeGuide — 2026 Pressure Washing Prices (average $170–$310, most homeowners around $210; house / siding $170–$360; driveway $100–$260; deck or patio $200–$240; fence $180–$300; roof $250–$600; pressure washing $0.08–$0.20 per sq ft; power washing $0.35–$0.77 per sq ft — national figures, labeled national) (homeguide.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-01 via Supabase: 6 active Pressure washing businesses serve the Omaha metro, all covering ZIP 68105 (Midtown Omaha), each with a logo on file and a single service ZIP; featured business Big Red Power Washing, Pressure washing, ZIP 68105, logo on file. The coverage grid listed 7 for this cell; the live count is 6.</div>'
