      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Sioux Falls homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Sioux Falls and South Dakota pages:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Standard cleaning, Sioux Falls (MaidProfit, Sioux Falls row)</td><td>$105–$225</td></tr><tr><td>Cleaner by the hour, Sioux Falls (MaidProfit, Sioux Falls row)</td><td>$23–$38 per cleaner</td></tr><tr><td>House cleaning overall, Sioux Falls (Janitorial Service Bids, Sioux Falls page)</td><td>$113–$245, or $0.09–$0.15 per sq ft</td></tr><tr><td>Home under 1,000 sq ft, Sioux Falls (Janitorial Service Bids)</td><td>$152–$247</td></tr><tr><td>Home 1,001–2,000 sq ft, Sioux Falls (Janitorial Service Bids)</td><td>$154–$256</td></tr><tr><td>Home 2,001–4,000 sq ft, Sioux Falls (Janitorial Service Bids)</td><td>$174–$323</td></tr><tr><td>Standard cleaning, South Dakota (MaidProfit, statewide)</td><td>$95–$215, average $150</td></tr><tr><td>Deep cleaning, South Dakota (MaidProfit, statewide)</td><td>$210–$415</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out cleaning, South Dakota (MaidProfit, statewide)</td><td>$235–$450</td></tr><tr><td>Maid hired directly, Sioux Falls (Care.com, Nov 2026)</td><td>$16/hr average posted rate</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Sioux Falls is the priciest cleaning market in South Dakota — biggest city, strongest demand (MaidProfit). The statewide standard average of $150 still sits 21% under the $190 national average on the same page. So a $225 Sioux Falls quote isn\'t a coastal price. It\'s the top of a low-cost state.</p><p>This is where people overpay: the first visit. A first clean on a home that hasn\'t been touched in months is priced like a deep clean, $210–$415 statewide. If a company quotes you deep-clean money and calls it a standard first visit, ask what the second visit costs. That number tells you the real rate.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Sioux Falls?</h3><p><strong>Winter, mostly.</strong> South Dakota winters mean snow, mud and road salt tracked across your floors for months (MaidProfit). Entryways and mudrooms in ZIPs 57103 through 57110 take the beating, and a spring booking after a full winter of grit is a longer job than the same rooms in July.</p><p><strong>Frequency.</strong> Recurring visits cost less statewide: weekly $80–$180, biweekly $85–$195, monthly $100–$215 (MaidProfit). The cleaner knows your home, and the buildup never gets ahead of them.</p><p><strong>Size and bathrooms.</strong> The per-square-foot figures on the Sioux Falls cost page run $0.09–$0.15, and the size table climbs from $152–$247 under 1,000 sq ft to $174–$323 at 2,001–4,000 sq ft. Bathrooms carry the scrubbing time, so a 3-bed, 3-bath prices above a 3-bed, 2-bath at the same square footage.</p><p><strong>Tax is on top.</strong> Cleaning services are taxable in South Dakota — 4.5% state tax plus local tax, 6.5% total in Sioux Falls (MaidProfit). A $150 quote can land at about $160 on the invoice. Ask whether your quote already includes it.</p><h3>Company crew or a person you hire yourself?</h3><p>At $16 an hour on Care.com, a listed individual costs well under a company\'s $23–$38 per cleaner. The trade-off is simple. If that person is sick or on vacation, nobody comes. A company sends a replacement, brings supplies, and carries the insurance. Plenty of households hire the individual and accept the gaps. Just price the gaps honestly.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get a good clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Go recurring after the first visit.</strong> Weekly and biweekly rates run well under one-time prices statewide. Pay the higher first-visit price once, then let the cheaper schedule hold it.</li><li><strong>Name the extras before the visit.</strong> Inside the oven, inside the fridge, interior windows — say it up front. Add-ons named mid-clean get priced mid-clean.</li><li><strong>Don\'t stop at the city line.</strong> Van Squads lists house cleaning across Sioux Falls ZIPs 57103–57110 and out to Brandon (57005), Harrisburg (57032) and Tea (57064). In a newer subdivision out that way, you still have local options — no need for a cleaner driving in from across town.</li><li><strong>Clear the entryway in winter.</strong> Boots and mats piled by the door eat paid minutes. A clear mudroom is a cheaper clean.</li></ul><h3>A Sioux Falls house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Emerald Cleaning of Sioux Falls</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location across Sioux Falls ZIPs 57103, 57104, 57105, 57106, 57107, 57108 and 57110. See its listing: <a href="/business/emerald-cleaning-of-sioux-falls">Emerald Cleaning of Sioux Falls on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 19 house cleaning businesses in the Sioux Falls metro: <a href="/#/browse?zip=57103">search house cleaning near 57103</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/house-cleaning/sioux-falls/">House cleaning in Sioux Falls</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Comparing metros? See the Omaha house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-omaha/">How much does house cleaning cost in Omaha?</a> and the Boise house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-boise/">How much does house cleaning cost in Boise?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> MaidProfit — How Much Do Cleaning Services Cost in South Dakota? (Sioux Falls row: hourly rate $23–$38 per cleaner, standard home cleaning $105–$225; Sioux Falls has the highest rates in the state as its largest city and economic center; statewide standard cleaning $95–$215, average $150, deep cleaning $210–$415, move-out cleaning $235–$450, recurring weekly $80–$180, biweekly $85–$195, monthly $100–$215; South Dakota standard average $150 vs national average $190, 21% lower; South Dakota winters track in snow, mud and road salt; South Dakota charges 4.5% state sales tax on cleaning services plus local taxes; a growing rental market in Sioux Falls) (maidprofit.com); MaidProfit — How to Start a Cleaning Business in South Dakota (cleaning services are taxable; state rate 4.5%, Sioux Falls adds a 2% local tax for a total of 6.5%) (maidprofit.com); Care.com — Find Maids Near Me in Sioux Falls, SD (2 maids listed in Sioux Falls; average posted rate $16.00/hr as of November 2026; FAQ: maids near Sioux Falls charge $16.50 per hour on average) (care.com); Janitorial Service Bids — How Much Does House Cleaning Cost in Sioux Falls, SD? (house cleaning in Sioux Falls generally $113–$245, or $0.09–$0.15 per square foot; by size: 0–1,000 sq ft $152–$247, 1,001–2,000 sq ft $154–$256, 2,001–4,000 sq ft $174–$323) (janitorialservicebids.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-02 via Supabase: 19 active House cleaning businesses serve the Sioux Falls metro (Sioux Falls ZIPs 57103, 57104, 57105, 57106, 57107, 57108, 57110, plus Brandon 57005, Harrisburg 57032 and Tea 57064 in some service areas), each with a logo on file; featured business Emerald Cleaning of Sioux Falls, House cleaning, ZIPs 57103, 57104, 57105, 57106, 57107, 57108, 57110, logo on file. The coverage grid listed 16 for this cell; the live count is 19.</div>'
