      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Portland drivers actually pay</h3><p>Published Portland prices — three mobile lists, one Tigard shop list, and national figures labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full detail, sedan / SUV or truck / large SUV (Bridge City, mobile)</td><td>$250 / $300 / $350</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail (Royal Detailing PDX, mobile)</td><td>$240</td></tr><tr><td>Exterior / interior detail (Royal)</td><td>$140 / $180</td></tr><tr><td>Interior only (Bridge City, mobile)</td><td>$150–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail, starting — car / SUV or truck / large (Mad Dog, mobile)</td><td>$480 / $600 / $660</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail, starting — car (Mad Dog, mobile)</td><td>$250</td></tr><tr><td>Complete detail, cars / SUVs and trucks / vans (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$269–$359 / $295–$385 / $325–$415</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail, cars (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$169–$249</td></tr><tr><td>Engine detailing (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$85</td></tr><tr><td>Ceramic coating, starting — car (Mad Dog)</td><td>$800</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile detailing, national average (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$144–$254</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $240 full detail and a $480 full detail aren’t two prices for the same work. Mad Dog’s $480 adds a one-step paint correction and paint protection to the inside-and-out clean. If your paint is fine and the cabin is the mess, that’s correction you never asked for. Read what’s in the package before you compare the number.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Portland?</h3><p><strong>Rain, sap, and moss set the Portland list.</strong> Armor Auto Detailing, a Portland-area mobile operator, puts it plainly: rain, road spray, tree sap, and mineral deposits leave paint dull even after a wash — and that’s before moss and pollen. Ace Cars in Tigard sets its final price by the same stuff — pet hair, water spots, tree sap, road tar, and paint oxidation are all named factors. Sap isn’t a quick wipe. It adds time, and time is the price.</p><p><strong>Size first, then condition.</strong> Bridge City charges $250, $300, or $350 by size alone, and says heavily soiled interiors and extreme pet hair may run higher, confirmed before work starts. Mad Dog prices pet hair removal as an add-on at $40 an hour and odor removal at $100. A clean sedan and a Tigard SUV that hauls a wet dog all winter aren’t the same job at any shop in town.</p><p><strong>Mobile in the rain is a real question here.</strong> Bridge City says interior details are generally possible rain or shine, though cover helps, and exterior work gets rescheduled if the forecast turns into a real downpour. Ask before you book a November appointment, not the morning of.</p><p><strong>Who brings water and power changes who can take the job.</strong> Bridge City needs a power outlet and, for exterior work, a hose at your place — interior-only can run without one. Royal says you need to provide nothing. In a Tigard apartment lot (97223), that difference decides the booking.</p><p><strong>Protection before the wet months pays back.</strong> Armor notes protection added after a clean helps grime release faster in the wet months — the car stays cleaner, and the next wash is cheaper work. A sealant added to a Tigard complete detail runs $80 at Ace Cars.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse detail</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Buy the half that’s dirty.</strong> Interior-only runs $150–$250 at Bridge City and $180 at Royal. Exterior-only is $140 at Royal. A full detail is the wrong buy when one side is fine.</li><li><strong>Describe the car honestly before you book.</strong> Ace Cars gives an approximate price from a good description — age, dirt, pet hair, stains, sap — and sets the final price at the appointment. Photos do the same job.</li><li><strong>Skip the correction if the paint doesn’t need it.</strong> A flat full detail at $240–$350 covers the clean. Correction and ceramic work start at $480 and $800 at Mad Dog — worth it on a car you keep, hard to justify on one you’re selling soon.</li><li><strong>Ask about water and power up front.</strong> Tell the detailer what your driveway or lot has. Surprises on the day cost more than the question.</li></ul><h3>A Portland mobile detailing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Squeegee Detail</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering mobile auto detailing at your location in Tigard (97223) and Tigard (97224). See its listing: <a href="/business/squeegee-detail">Squeegee Detail on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 6 mobile auto detailing businesses in the Portland metro: <a href="/#/browse?zip=97223">search mobile detailing near 97223</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/mobile-auto-detailing/portland/">Mobile auto detailing in Portland</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>House needs work too? See the Portland house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-portland/">How much does house cleaning cost in Portland?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Sioux Falls mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-sioux-falls/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Sioux Falls?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Bridge City Detailing — Mobile Auto Detailing in Portland, OR (Portland mobile operator, flat pricing with no add-on menu: full detail $250 sedan, $300 SUV/4-door including crossovers and trucks, $350 large SUV; interior only $150–$250 by vehicle size and condition, including vacuum, wipe-down, windows and glass, mats cleaned, deodorize; prices reflect typical condition, heavily soiled interiors, extreme pet hair, or certain extra-large vehicles may run slightly higher and are confirmed before work starts; full details run about 2–3 hours, interior-only 1–2 hours; needs driveway space, a power outlet, and hose access for exterior details, interior-only possible without a hose; interior details generally possible rain or shine with cover preferred, exterior work rescheduled for a real downpour; serves the Portland metro including Tigard) (bridgecitydetailing.org); Mad Dog Auto Detailing — Mobile Car Detailing Portland, OR (Portland mobile operator: Interior Detail starts at $250 for cars, $275 SUVs/trucks, $325 large SUVs/trucks; Exterior Detail with paint enhancement starts at $275, $325 SUVs/trucks, $350 large; Full Detail starts at $480, $600 SUVs/trucks, $660 large, including full interior and exterior detail, one-step paint correction, and paint protection, about 4 hours — Mad Dog’s page gives the protection term as 6 months on the service card and 6 weeks in its FAQ text, so no term is quoted in this post; Express interior and exterior detail from $250, $300 SUVs/trucks, $360 large, about 2 hours; add-ons: excessive pet hair $40/hr, engine bay detail $80+, odor removal $100, biohazard cleanup $100; 2-year ceramic coating with one-step paint correction starts at $800 for cars, $1,000 SUVs/trucks, $1,200 large; final price depends on vehicle condition, heavy pet hair or stains can cost more) (maddogdetails.com); Royal Detailing PDX — Portland, OR (Portland mobile operator, all services mobile: exterior detail $140 including hand wash, wheel and tire cleaning, tire dressing; interior detail $180 including deep vacuum, surface wipe-down, stain treatment, windows and mirrors; full detail $240, complete interior and exterior; premium services starting at $240 with clay bar, ceramic sealant, steam cleaning; ceramic coating starting at $900; headlight restoration starting at $140; exterior or interior detail about 1–2 hours, full detail 3–4 hours; customer provides nothing; serves the Portland metro including Tigard) (royaldetailingpdx.com); Ace Cars — Tigard Auto Detailing, Tigard, OR (Tigard shop list: Complete Detail $269–$359 cars and wagons, $295–$385 SUVs and trucks, $325–$415 vans; Interior Detail $169–$249 cars, $189–$269 SUVs and trucks, $195–$275 vans; Exterior Detail same ranges as interior; Paint Sealant Package $80 added to a complete detail; engine detailing $85; touchup paint $65–$85; odor removal $50–$100; final price determined by size of vehicle, general dirt, pet hair, water spots, tree sap, road tar, paint oxidation, food/beverage spills, and carpet and upholstery stains; an approximate price can be given from a good description of the car, final price set at the appointment; full detail takes about 7 hours at the shop) (acecars.net); Armor Auto Detailing — Exterior Services, Wilsonville, OR (Portland-area mobile operator: PNW weather is rough on exterior surfaces — rain, road spray, tree sap, and mineral deposits can leave paint looking dull even after a wash; Portland drivers deal with constant rain and tree sap to moss, pollen, and road grime; adding protection after cleaning helps grime release faster, a major upgrade in wet PNW months, so the vehicle stays cleaner with less effort; before winter, adding protection helps grime release faster during washes, after winter a reset brings back gloss; serves Tigard and the Portland metro) (armorautodetailing.com); Thumbtack — 2026 Mobile Car Detailing Prices (national average $144–$254, low-end $95, high-end $390; price depends on vehicle size, condition, service package, and location — national figures, labeled national) (thumbtack.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-04 via Supabase: 6 active Mobile auto detailing businesses serve the Portland metro, all covering Tigard ZIP 97223 (6 listings); plus Tigard 97224: 1 covered by the featured business — businesses covering several ZIPs count in each, distinct total 6, each with a logo on file. Featured business Squeegee Detail, Mobile auto detailing, ZIPs 97223 and 97224, logo on file. The coverage grid listed 6 for this cell; the live count is 6.</div>'
