      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Denver drivers actually pay</h3><p>Published Denver-area prices — four mobile lists and national figures labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full detail, starting (Euro Mile High 5280, mobile)</td><td>$179.99</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail, starting — sedan (Creek, mobile)</td><td>$249</td></tr><tr><td>Interior & exterior — sedan / SUV / 3-row or truck (All In, mobile)</td><td>$150 / $200 / $250</td></tr><tr><td>Premium, with stain extraction — sedan / SUV / 3-row / truck (All In)</td><td>$300 / $340 / $380 / $400</td></tr><tr><td>Basic interior — sedan / SUV / 3-row or truck (All In)</td><td>$100 / $120 / $140</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail — car / SUV / truck or van (PEAK, Aurora & Denver)</td><td>$110 / $140 / $170</td></tr><tr><td>Exterior detail — car / SUV / truck or van (PEAK)</td><td>$90 / $120 / $150</td></tr><tr><td>Interior / exterior detail, starting (Creek)</td><td>$149 / $129</td></tr><tr><td>Premium finish with machine polish, starting (Creek Reserve)</td><td>$449</td></tr><tr><td>Paint enhancement / ceramic protection, starting (Creek)</td><td>$349 / $699</td></tr><tr><td>Paint correction, starting (Euro Mile High 5280)</td><td>$329</td></tr><tr><td>Pet hair — All In (flat add) / PEAK (add-on)</td><td>+$50 / $20</td></tr><tr><td>Engine bay wipe-down (PEAK)</td><td>$25</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile detailing, national average (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$144–$254</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $179.99 full detail and a $449 premium finish are not the same job at two prices. The $449 Creek Reserve adds clay and iron decontamination, a machine polish, and premium paint protection on top of the clean. If your paint looks fine and the cabin is the mess, buy the cabin work.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Denver?</h3><p><strong>Altitude sun works on your paint all year.</strong> Denver Auto Shield, a Denver protection shop, puts it bluntly: Denver is a mile closer to the sun, with roughly 300 days of sunshine a year, and that UV load oxidizes clear coat and fades pigment. That’s why protection shows up on so many Denver lists — Creek prices paint enhancement from $349 and ceramic protection from $699, and Euro Mile High starts paint correction at $329. On a car you plan to keep, that work has a point here. On one you’re selling this spring, it usually doesn’t.</p><p><strong>Winter leaves a film you can see.</strong> Denver Auto Shield says winter roads here get covered in rocks and salt and drenched in mag chloride, and people clean their cars less in the cold, so the stuff sits and bonds to the paint. Jazz It Up, in Centennial, calls the residue a filmy white spray down the doors and rocker panels, and says to wash with pH-balanced soap after mag-chloride exposure. A spring detail in University Park (80210) or Saddle Rock in Aurora (80016) is often priced by how much of that film has to come off first.</p><p><strong>Size first, then condition.</strong> All In’s ladder is plain: $150, $200, $250 by size for the same job. PEAK runs $110 to $170 for an interior by size. Creek says size, condition, and add-on adjustments are quoted before service, and heavy pet hair or staining can mean an added charge.</p><p><strong>Pet hair is priced three different ways in this metro.</strong> All In adds a flat $50 on its basic and interior-and-exterior packages, then includes removal in its premium package. PEAK lists it at $20. Creek quotes it case by case. Same dog, three prices — ask which rule your detailer uses before you book.</p><p><strong>Who brings water and power decides where the job can happen.</strong> Creek says its setup is self-contained for most appointments, and it will tell you before booking if a job needs your water or power. PEAK says it may need an outdoor hookup and an outlet, confirmed before the appointment. In an apartment lot in University Park, that difference decides the booking.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse detail</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Buy the half that’s dirty.</strong> Interior-only starts at $100–$149 on the lists above, exterior-only at $90–$129. A full detail is the wrong buy when one side is fine.</li><li><strong>Name the pet hair up front.</strong> It’s $20 at PEAK, $50 at All In, and a custom quote at Creek. Naming it early keeps the quote you were given.</li><li><strong>Time the big detail for spring.</strong> Getting the winter film off early is cleaning work. Leaving it bonded another season turns it into correction work, and correction starts at $329–$349.</li><li><strong>Ask about water and power before you book.</strong> Tell the detailer what your driveway or lot has.</li></ul><h3>A Denver mobile detailing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Mile High Shine</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering mobile auto detailing at your location in University Park, Denver (80210). See its listing: <a href="/business/mile-high-shine">Mile High Shine on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 16 mobile auto detailing businesses in the Denver metro: <a href="/#/browse?zip=80210">search mobile detailing near 80210</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/mobile-auto-detailing/denver/">Mobile auto detailing in Denver</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Comparing metros? See the Portland mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-portland/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Portland?</a> and the Sioux Falls mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-sioux-falls/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Sioux Falls?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> Creek Mobile Detail — Denver Mobile Car Detailing (Denver mobile operator: interior detail from $149, exterior detail from $129, full detail from $249, paint enhancement from $349, ceramic protection from $699; Refresh $149 starting, Signature $249 starting, Reserve $449 starting with clay and iron decontamination, machine polish and premium paint protection; sedan/coupe table from $149 / $249 / $449, SUV, truck and van by custom quote; pricing varies by vehicle size and condition; pet hair, shampoo, ozone, headlights and engine-bay work by custom quote, heavy pet hair or staining may mean an added charge; mobile setup designed to be self-contained for most appointments, with any water or power need stated before booking; most appointments about 1.5 to 4 hours; serves Denver, Aurora, Lakewood, Centennial, Parker, Greenwood Village, Englewood, Littleton and nearby Front Range communities) (creekmobiledetail.com); All In Detailing — Mobile Auto Detailing Denver (Denver mobile operator serving Denver, Lakewood, Aurora and Arvada: Basic Interior Detail $100 sedan, $120 SUV, $140 3-row SUV, $140 truck, pet hair not included; pet hair adds $50 on Basic and Interior & Exterior; Interior & Exterior $150 sedan, $200 SUV, $250 3-row SUV, $250 truck; Premium Package $300 sedan, $340 SUV, $380 3-row SUV, $400 truck, including stain extraction on all seats and carpet and pet hair removal) (allindetl.com); PEAK Auto Detailing — Mobile Car Detailing in Aurora & Denver (Aurora-based mobile operator serving Denver and the Front Range: interior detail car $110, SUV $140, truck/van $170 starting; exterior detail car $90, SUV $120, truck/van $150 starting; pet hair removal $20 add-on; engine bay wipe down $25; ceramic coating and 2-step paint correction by quote; most details around 2–4 hours; may need an outdoor water hookup and electrical outlet depending on service and location, confirmed before the appointment; full detail recommended every 3–6 months for most vehicles; weather that makes a detail impossible is rescheduled) (peakautodetailing.org); Euro Mile High 5280 Mobile Detail — Denver Car Detailing (Denver mobile operator: Basic Wash & Shine starting at $69, Full Detail starting at $179.99 including clay bar treatment, hand wax and polish, deep interior clean, leather conditioning and odor elimination, Premium Paint Correction starting at $329; brings its full setup to your home, office, or anywhere in the Denver metro) (euromilehigh5280.com); Denver Auto Shield — The Top 3 Things That Want to Destroy Your Paint in CO (Denver protection shop: rock chips, UV exposure and winter weather are the three biggest paint factors in Colorado; Denver is a mile closer to the sun with roughly 300 days of sunshine a year, UV oxidizes clear coat and fades pigment; winter roads are covered in rocks and salt and drenched in mag chloride, people clean cars less in the cold so contaminants sit, settle into the paint and bond) (denverautoshield.com); Jazz It Up Truck & Auto Accessories — How Clear Bra Protects Your Vehicle from Colorado Roads, Centennial, CO (Colorado roads source: winter gravel, magnesium chloride, hot sun and construction zones damage paint; mag-chloride residue is slightly corrosive, can etch clear coat if it sits, and shows as a filmy white spray down the doors and rocker panels; wash with pH-balanced soap after mag-chloride exposure; serves Denver, Aurora, Englewood and Lone Tree) (jazzituptruckandauto.com); Thumbtack — 2026 Mobile Car Detailing Prices (national average $144–$254, low-end $95, high-end $390; price depends on vehicle size, condition, service package, and location — national figures, labeled national) (thumbtack.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-05 via Supabase: 16 active Mobile auto detailing businesses serve the Denver metro — 8 covering University Park, Denver ZIP 80210 and 8 covering Saddle Rock, Aurora ZIP 80016; every listing in this cell carries a single service ZIP, each with a logo on file. Featured business Mile High Shine, Mobile auto detailing, ZIP 80210, logo on file. The coverage grid listed 16 for this cell; the live count is 16.</div>'
