      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Denver homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Denver pages, plus one national row labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>House wash, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$170–$420 (avg $295)</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, 1,500–2,000 sq ft house, Denver (HomeBlue)</td><td>$400–$700 (avg ~$600)</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, full exterior, Denver metro operator (Colorado Choice)</td><td>$300–$600</td></tr><tr><td>Average property, Denver operator (Window Genie)</td><td>$200–$500</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway, 40 x 20 ft, Denver (HomeBlue)</td><td>$160–$290 (avg ~$230)</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$100–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway, Denver metro operator (Colorado Choice)</td><td>$150–$350</td></tr><tr><td>Deck or patio, 200 sq ft, Denver (HomeBlue)</td><td>$70–$110 (avg ~$90)</td></tr><tr><td>Deck, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$100–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Patio, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$100–$200</td></tr><tr><td>Patio or sidewalk, Denver metro operator (Colorado Choice)</td><td>$100–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Fence, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$150–$300</td></tr><tr><td>Pressure washing, per sq ft, Denver (Angi)</td><td>$0.10–$0.50</td></tr><tr><td>House / siding wash (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$170–$360</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $295 quote and a $600 quote for "a house wash" can both be real. One is Angi\'s surveyed Denver average, the other is HomeBlue\'s average for a 1,500 to 2,000 sq ft house. Ask what each one measured — house size, stories, or square feet of wall. Thumbtack\'s Denver per-square-foot figure is per square foot of your property size, not of the surface washed.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Denver?</h3><p><strong>Winter road chemicals, mostly.</strong> A Denver metro operator puts it plainly: magnesium chloride and calcium chloride go on metro roads from October through April, get tracked onto driveways, and corrode concrete if they sit there. That\'s why the spring wash in Lakewood (80226) isn\'t just about looks. It\'s getting a corrosive film off before another freeze-thaw season works it into cracks.</p><p><strong>The Front Range adds its own grime.</strong> The same operator lists red clay soil that bonds hard to concrete, hard to very hard Denver water that leaves a white mineral haze, and high-altitude sun that roughens surfaces so they trap more dirt. A driveway with white haze and clay staining is pre-treatment and dwell time, not a quick rinse — and it prices that way.</p><p><strong>Stories and size set the base.</strong> HomeBlue climbs by house size, up to $1,000 to $1,800 at 4,000 to 5,000 sq ft. Angi prices two-story Denver homes at $400 to $1,400 against $150 to $1,000 for one story. Height, tight access, and limited water access push a quote up.</p><p><strong>The surface decides the method, and the method sets the price.</strong> Angi prices Denver work by material per square foot: brick $0.10 to $0.40, vinyl $0.20 to $0.50, stucco $0.30 to $0.50, wood $0.30 to $0.55. Concrete takes high pressure. Siding gets a soft wash — lower pressure, with the cleaning mix doing the work — because a hard blast can damage it.</p><h3>Should you pay for hot water?</h3><p>Sometimes. HomeBlue notes power washing — heated water — costs 10 to 15% more than its cold-water Denver prices. The Denver metro operator uses hot water at 180 to 200°F and says it earns that on oil and grease, where cold water alone can\'t lift the stain, and on road-chemical residue.</p><p>On plain dust and winter film, it usually doesn\'t earn it. Angi\'s Denver pros charge $50 to $150 an hour, and renting a machine yourself runs $50 to $250 a day — before you count your own Saturday. If the quote adds a hot-water charge, ask which stain it is for.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get it clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Bundle surfaces in one visit.</strong> House, driveway, and front walk in one stop — the crew is already set up. A 200 sq ft deck or patio runs $70 to $110 as its own job on HomeBlue; as an add-on it should cost less.</li><li><strong>Wash in spring, after the road-chemical season.</strong> Angi puts the best window at March to November, with driveways in spring or fall — spring in Denver means after the last mag chloride, not before it.</li><li><strong>Get the measuring stick in writing.</strong> By house size, by story, or per square foot — and per square foot of what? The two Denver guides differ mostly on this, not on the work.</li><li><strong>Send photos of the worst spots.</strong> The white mineral haze, the clay-stained edge, the oil spot by the garage in Lakewood (80226). A photo quote beats a surprise on the day.</li></ul><h3>A Denver pressure washing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Denver Pressure Washing</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering pressure washing at your location in Lakewood (80226). See its listing: <a href="/business/denver-pressure-washing">Denver Pressure Washing on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 8 pressure washing businesses in the Denver metro: <a href="/#/browse?zip=80226">search pressure washing near 80226</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/pressure-washing/denver/">Pressure washing in Denver</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>House needs work too? See the Denver house cleaning cost guide: <a href=\"/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-denver/\">How much does house cleaning cost in Denver?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Portland pressure washing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-pressure-washing-cost-in-portland/">How much does pressure washing cost in Portland?</a> and the Denver mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-denver/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Denver?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> HomeBlue — Pressure Washing Prices in Denver, Colorado (overall Denver range $70–$1,800 by task; house average ~$600, $400–$700 for a 1,500–2,000 sq ft house, $600–$1,100 at 2,000–3,000 sq ft, $800–$1,400 at 3,000–4,000 sq ft, $1,000–$1,800 at 4,000–5,000 sq ft; driveway average ~$230, $160–$290 for a 40 x 20 ft / 800 sq ft driveway, $250–$430 at 1,200 sq ft, $330–$580 at 1,600 sq ft, $410–$720 at 2,000 sq ft; deck or patio average ~$90, $70–$110 for a 200 sq ft deck, $220–$340 at 600 sq ft, $290–$450 at 800 sq ft, $360–$570 at 1,000 sq ft; power washing with heated water costs 10–15% more than the guide\'s cold-water prices; price rises with two or more stories, difficult access, limited water access, heated water, landscaping in the work area, and significant dirt, mold, and mildew) (homeblue.com); Angi — How Much Does It Cost to Pressure Wash a House in Denver, CO? (Denver house wash $170–$420, average $295, about 5% less than the national average; pressure washing $0.10–$0.50 per sq ft in Denver; by home size: 1,500 sq ft $150–$750, 2,000 sq ft $200–$1,000, 2,500 sq ft $250–$1,250; by project: deck $100–$250, driveway $100–$250, patio $100–$200, fence $150–$300, siding $150–$1,400; by stories: one $150–$1,000, two $400–$1,400, three $700–$1,800; by material per sq ft: brick $0.10–$0.40, stucco $0.30–$0.50, wood $0.30–$0.55, vinyl $0.20–$0.50; hiring a pro in Denver $50–$150 per hour; renting a pressure washer $50–$250 per day; Denver sales tax 9.15%, about $25 on a typical job; pressure wash once per year, best time March to November, siding spring or fall, driveway spring or fall after winter snow or fall leaves; Denver\'s semi-arid climate, high winds, and proximity to dusty regions can mean more dirt buildup) (angi.com); Colorado Choice — Pressure Washing Denver Metro (Denver metro operator: residential driveway cleaning $150–$350 by size and contamination, patios and sidewalks $100–$250, full exterior house washing $300–$600 by square footage and siding type; magnesium chloride and calcium chloride applied to Denver metro roads from October through April are tracked onto driveways and corrode concrete; Front Range red clay soil bonds aggressively to concrete and masonry; Denver metro water is hard to very hard and deposits calcium and magnesium as white or gray haze; high-altitude UV accelerates surface oxidation, making surfaces rougher and more porous; freeze-thaw cycling enlarges cracks that trap contamination; commercial hot water at 180 to 200°F with pre-treatment, 2,000 to 3,500 PSI on concrete by age and condition and 2,500 to 3,500 PSI for concrete and masonry in its process steps, 1,500 to 2,000 PSI / soft washing for siding and wood, with a pre-wash assessment and advice if existing damage would be worsened; cold water alone cannot emulsify oil stains; annual driveway washing is the standard recommendation, spring cleaning after winter road treatment removes corrosive residue) (coloradochoicecarpet.com); Window Genie — Pressure Washing Service in Denver, CO (Denver operator: budget $200 to $500 for an average property; pressure washing your home\'s exterior every 12–18 months is generally advisable) (windowgenie.com); Thumbtack — The Best Pressure Cleaners in Denver, CO (some Denver pressure washers have starting costs as low as $85; pressure washing about $0.10–$0.17 per square foot of your property size; ask the pro how much they charge per square foot of the surface itself for driveways, decks, fences, and roofs) (thumbtack.com); HomeGuide — 2026 Pressure Washing Prices (average $170–$310, most homeowners around $210; house / siding $170–$360; driveway $100–$260; deck or patio $200–$240; fence $180–$300; roof $250–$600 — national figures, labeled national) (homeguide.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-05 via Supabase: 8 active Pressure washing businesses serve the Denver metro, all covering Lakewood ZIP 80226 (8 listings) — Denver Pressure Washing, A Good Front Window Cleaning & Pressure Washing, Top Notch Gutter Services, Platinum Pressure Washing, Squeegee Squad - Denver County, CO, Mile High Mobile Wash, Sparkle Squad of NW Denver-Arvada-Broomfield-Golden, and Professional Window Cleaning; every listing has a logo on file. Featured business Denver Pressure Washing, Pressure washing, ZIP 80226 (Lakewood), logo on file, not previously featured. The coverage grid listed 8 for this cell; the live count is 8.</div>'
