      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Denver homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Published Denver prices — city guides, two Denver operators, and national figures labeled national:</p><table class=\"price-table\"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Standard clean, average per visit (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$176</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, most pros (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$119–$234</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean (MaidProfit, Denver row)</td><td>$150–$300</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, per cleaner (MaidProfit, Denver row)</td><td>$30–$50</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, average (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$45 (range $25–$75)</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, starting rate (Care.com, Denver)</td><td>$24.62/hr (max avg $29.34/hr)</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, per sq ft (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$0.12–$0.25</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 1,500 sq ft home (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$180–$375</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring visit, most clients (Alpine Maids, Denver)</td><td>$150–$360</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring, 3 bed / 2.5 bath / 2,400 sq ft, biweekly (Alpine Maids)</td><td>$245</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring visit, by size (Kathy Clean, Denver metro, Oct 2026)</td><td>$129–$469</td></tr><tr><td>One-time clean, under 4,000 sq ft (Mile High Maid, Denver)</td><td>$155–$425</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, 4 hours (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$180–$300</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, by size (Kathy Clean, Denver metro)</td><td>$345–$835</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, 1,800 sq ft home (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$540</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out clean, 1,800 sq ft home (Angi, Denver)</td><td>$720</td></tr><tr><td>Standard / deep clean, national (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$90–$180 / $230–$600</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $176 average visit and a $540 deep clean are not the same job at two prices. The deep clean is priced per square foot at about $0.30 on Angi\'s Denver page, against $0.12 to $0.25 for a standard clean, because it adds the built-up work a regular visit skips. If your home gets a regular clean already, you probably need the regular price.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Denver?</h3><p><strong>Dry air means dust comes back fast.</strong> MaidProfit\'s Colorado page says it plain: the high altitude and dry climate mean homes here accumulate dust quickly, and that pushes people toward regular cleaning instead of one-off visits. In Hilltop (80220) and Windsor Gardens (80224), that shows up as a biweekly rhythm — Alpine\'s $245 example home is priced on a two-week cycle, not monthly.</p><p><strong>How the company counts your home matters more than the headline rate.</strong> Alpine Maids prices flat by bedrooms and bathrooms, and says the price only changes on arrival for an obvious problem like a hoarding or post-party cleanup. Angi\'s Denver pros price by the square foot. Care.com\'s Denver cleaners price by the hour. Same house, three ways of counting — a 2,400 sq ft home can look cheap by the hour and pricey by the square foot. Get the counting method in writing before you compare two quotes.</p><p><strong>Frequency is the discount.</strong> Kathy Clean\'s Denver table runs recurring visits from $129 for a small home, while its one-time deep cleans for the same metro run $345 to $835 by size. Mile High Maid, another Denver operator, prices a one-time clean at $155 to $425 and a deep clean at $250 to $430. A first visit costs more because it\'s doing catch-up work. The second and third visits are the cheaper ones.</p><p><strong>Move-out is its own price tier.</strong> Angi puts a move-out clean for a 1,800 sq ft Denver home at $720, up to $0.40 a square foot, and a pre-sale deep clean at $540 to $720 or more. That\'s empty-home work — inside cabinets, inside appliances, baseboards a deposit inspection actually checks. Don\'t budget a move-out from the standard-clean average.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse clean</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Start recurring, even if it\'s monthly.</strong> The Denver tables above price repeat visits well under one-time work for the same home.</li><li><strong>Ask which counting method the quote uses.</strong> Flat by bed and bath, per square foot, and per hour reward different homes. A small home with many bathrooms pays more under bed-and-bath pricing.</li><li><strong>Name the extras before the visit.</strong> Oven and fridge interiors are deep-clean or add-on work on the Denver lists, not part of a standard visit.</li><li><strong>Keep the first visit honest.</strong> If the home hasn\'t been cleaned in months, say so. A crew that arrives expecting a standard clean and finds a deep clean reprices on the spot.</li></ul><h3>A Denver house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Alpine Maids</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location in Hilltop, Denver (80220) and Windsor Gardens, Denver (80224). See its listing: <a href=\"/business/alpine-maids\">Alpine Maids on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 8 house cleaning businesses in the Denver metro — covering Hilltop (80220), Windsor Gardens (80224), Downtown Denver (80202), and University Hills (80222): <a href=\"/#/browse?zip=80220\">search house cleaning near 80220</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/house-cleaning/denver/\">House cleaning in Denver</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Car needs work too? See the Denver mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href=\"/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-denver/\">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Denver?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Portland house cleaning cost guide: <a href=\"/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-portland/\">How much does house cleaning cost in Portland?</a> and the Denver handyman cost guide: <a href=\"/blog/how-much-does-a-handyman-cost-in-denver/\">How much does a handyman cost in Denver?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class=\"disclosure\"><strong>Sources.</strong> Angi — How Much Does Professional House Cleaning Cost in Denver, CO? (Denver guide, updated Oct 24, 2025: average $176 per visit, most pros $119–$234; hourly average about $45, ranging $25–$75; standard cleans $0.12–$0.25 per sq ft, so a 1,500 sq ft standard cleaning runs $180–$375; a four-hour deep cleaning runs about $180–$300; deep cleaning about $0.30 per sq ft and move-out up to $0.40 per sq ft; for a 1,800 sq ft home, deep $540 and move-out $720; a pre-sale deep clean runs $540 to $720 or more) (angi.com); Care.com — How much does house cleaning cost in Denver, CO? (Denver starting rate $24.62/hr, max rate average $29.34/hr; Colorado starting $23.42/hr; United States starting $21.66/hr; FAQ average about $24.63 per hour as of November 2026; rates vary by home size, frequency, and services requested, and deep, move-in or move-out cleanings and using the cleaner\'s own supplies affect the total) (care.com); MaidProfit — How Much Do Cleaning Services Cost in Colorado? (Denver row: hourly rate $30–$50 per cleaner, standard home cleaning $150–$300; Colorado standard cleaning $140–$290 statewide, hourly $28–$50; Colorado has the highest rates in Boulder and Denver; the high altitude and dry climate mean homes accumulate dust quickly, which increases demand for regular cleaning) (maidprofit.com); Alpine Maids — FAQs: House Cleaning Service Questions Answered (Denver operator: most clients pay $150–$360 per visit for recurring service; a 3 bed, 2.5 bath, 2,400 sq ft home averages $245 for service every two weeks; price is based on home size, frequency, and how much attention the home needs; flat-rate pricing by bedrooms and bathrooms, with prices affected on arrival only by an obvious cleaning problem such as hoarding or post-party cleanups; a deep clean is performed on the first visit to bring the home to maintenance condition) (alpinemaids.com); Kathy Clean — How Much Does House Cleaning Cost in Denver? (Denver metro flat rates as of October 2026: recurring plans priced per visit by square footage, most Denver metro homes between about $129 and $469 per visit for recurring cleaning depending on square footage and frequency; one-time deep cleans roughly $345 to $835 by home size, with deep $345 under 900 sq ft rising to $745–$835 at 4,701–6,000 sq ft; a biweekly professional visit starts around $145 flat-rate for smaller homes) (kathyclean.com); Mile High Maid Cleaning Co. — Book Denver-Area House Cleaning (Denver operator: one-time cleaning $155–$425 per visit for homes under 4,000 sq ft; deep cleaning $250–$430 per visit for homes under 2,500 sq ft — $250 under 1,000 sq ft, $305 at 1,000–1,499 sq ft, $370 at 1,500–1,999 sq ft, $430 at 2,000–2,499 sq ft; move-in/move-out cleaning $280–$415 per visit for homes under 2,000 sq ft, with appliance and cabinet interiors as separate extras) (milehighmaid.com); Thumbtack — The Best Cleaning in Denver, CO (Denver house cleaners on Thumbtack charge between $70 and $125 as starting costs; price is affected by number of bedrooms and bathrooms and by cleaning type, with deep and move-out cleanings priced differently; window, fridge and oven cleaning are extra-cost add-ons) (thumbtack.com); HomeGuide — House Cleaning Cost Guide (national figures, labeled national: a standard house cleaning costs $90 to $180 on average, and a deep cleaning costs $230 to $600; prices depend on home size and whether fridge cleaning, window cleaning, or other services are included; many services offer discounts for weekly or monthly cleanings) (homeguide.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-05 via Supabase: 8 active House cleaning businesses serve the Denver metro — Alpine Maids (ZIPs 80220, 80224), Wendy\'s Cleaning Service (80220, 80224), Broom (80220, 80202), The Haus Keepers (80220, 80222), Organic Maids (80220), Dream Clean Service (80220), Denver Mop Stars Cleaning Service (80220, 80202), and Denver Cleaning Service Company (80220, 80222); every listing has a logo on file. Featured business Alpine Maids, House cleaning, ZIPs 80220 (Hilltop, Denver) and 80224 (Windsor Gardens, Denver), logo on file, not previously featured. The coverage grid listed 8 for this cell; the live count is 8.</div>'
