      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Salt Lake City homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Published Salt Lake prices — city guides, two Salt Lake operators, and national figures labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Standard clean (MaidProfit, Salt Lake City row)</td><td>$135–$275</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, per cleaner (MaidProfit, Salt Lake City row)</td><td>$28–$46</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, average individual cleaner (Care.com, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$21.28/hr (starting $21.29, max avg $25.52)</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring Partial Clean, from, biweekly (Queen of Maids, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$149</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring Full Clean, from, biweekly (Queen of Maids)</td><td>$175</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring Full Premium, from, biweekly (Queen of Maids)</td><td>$225</td></tr><tr><td>One-time standard, apartment / 1–2 bed, from (Wasatch Cleaners, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$219</td></tr><tr><td>One-time standard, family home 3 bed, from (Wasatch Cleaners)</td><td>$289</td></tr><tr><td>One-time standard, large home 4–5 bed, from (Wasatch Cleaners)</td><td>$345</td></tr><tr><td>Recurring standard, from — weekly / biweekly / monthly (Wasatch Cleaners)</td><td>$186.15 / $197.10 / $208.05</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, from (Wasatch Cleaners)</td><td>$319</td></tr><tr><td>Move-in / move-out, from (Wasatch Cleaners)</td><td>$329</td></tr><tr><td>Maid service hourly (MaidThis, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$45–$55</td></tr><tr><td>Two-bedroom flat, per visit (MaidThis)</td><td>$120–$180</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, Utah average (MaidProfit, Utah)</td><td>$120–$260 (avg $180)</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, Utah range (MaidProfit, Utah)</td><td>$235–$475</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out clean, Utah range (MaidProfit, Utah)</td><td>$260–$510</td></tr><tr><td>Standard / deep clean, national (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$90–$180 / $230–$600</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, per cleaner, national (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$25–$50</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $149 biweekly Partial Clean and a $319 deep clean aren\'t the same job at two prices. The Partial covers the kitchen, bathrooms, floors, and trash in a home that already stays tidy. The deep clean adds the built-up work — behind appliances, baseboards, grout. If your home gets cleaned every two weeks, you need the $149 kind of price, not the $319 one.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Salt Lake City?</h3><p><strong>Inversion season puts dust inside your home.</strong> From December to February, warm air traps cold air in the Salt Lake Valley and the haze sits for days. Wolfnest\'s Utah rental guide notes that poor outdoor air in inversion season means more dust and particles settling indoors — on carpets, upholstery, ceiling fans, and vents. A home in West Valley City (84119) that keeps its windows shut for weeks still collects that film. Dusting that actually covers fans and vents is worth asking about before a winter booking.</p><p><strong>Utah homes run big, and big homes take longer.</strong> MaidProfit makes the point on its Utah page: the state has some of the largest average family sizes in the country, so homes are bigger and take more cleaning time. Wasatch Cleaners\' ladder shows it in dollars — $219 for a 1–2 bedroom place, $289 for a 3-bedroom family home, $345 for a 4–5 bedroom home, all in normal condition. Count bedrooms and bathrooms before you compare two quotes.</p><p><strong>How often you book is the discount.</strong> Wasatch Cleaners prices a one-time standard clean from $219, but recurring visits start lower: $186.15 weekly, $197.10 biweekly, $208.05 monthly. Queen of Maids builds its whole Salt Lake pricing around biweekly plans, from $149 to $225 depending on how much of the home is covered. MaidProfit\'s Utah ranges agree: weekly $100 to $215 a visit against $130 to $265 monthly.</p><p><strong>Deep and move-out work sits in its own tier.</strong> Wasatch Cleaners starts deep cleaning at $319 and move-in/move-out at $329, against $219 for a standard visit. MaidProfit\'s Utah ranges put deep cleans at $235 to $475 and move-outs at $260 to $510. Don\'t budget a move-out in Holladay (84124) from the standard-clean price — an empty home gets checked room by room, and the quote reflects that.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Go recurring, even monthly.</strong> Every Salt Lake list checked prices repeat visits under one-time work for the same home.</li><li><strong>Match the tier to the mess.</strong> A tidy home on a biweekly plan doesn\'t need the Premium tier with ceiling fans and vents every visit — save that for a seasonal deep clean.</li><li><strong>Say the home\'s real size up front.</strong> Bedrooms and bathrooms set the flat rate at both Salt Lake operators above. A surprise extra bathroom reprices the visit.</li><li><strong>Ask what inversion dust work is included.</strong> Fans, vents, and baseboards are deep-clean items on most lists. Naming them before you book is cheaper than adding them at the door.</li></ul><h3>A Salt Lake City house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>MaidPro Salt Lake City</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location in West Valley City (84119) and Holladay (84124). See its listing: <a href="/business/maidpro-salt-lake-city">MaidPro Salt Lake City on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 8 house cleaning businesses in the Salt Lake City metro — covering West Valley City (84119) and Holladay (84124): <a href="/#/browse?zip=84119">search house cleaning near 84119</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/house-cleaning/salt-lake-city/">House cleaning in Salt Lake City</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Car needs work too? See the Salt Lake City mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-salt-lake-city/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Salt Lake City?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Denver house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-denver/">How much does house cleaning cost in Denver?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> MaidProfit — How Much Do Cleaning Services Cost in Utah? (Utah page, published 2026-02-23, with a Salt Lake City row: hourly rate $28–$46 per cleaner, standard home cleaning $135–$275; Utah statewide: standard cleaning $120–$260, average $180, deep cleaning $235–$475, move-out cleaning $260–$510, recurring weekly $100–$215, biweekly $110–$235, monthly $130–$265; Utah has some of the largest average family sizes in the country, which means bigger homes that take more time to clean) (maidprofit.com); Care.com — How much does house cleaning cost in Salt Lake City, UT? (Salt Lake City starting rate $21.29/hr, max rate average $25.52/hr; Utah starting $19.68/hr; United States starting $21.66/hr; FAQ average about $21.28 per hour as of November 2026; rates vary by home size, frequency, and services requested, and deep, move-in or move-out cleanings and using the cleaner\'s own supplies affect the total) (care.com); Queen of Maids — House Cleaning Cost in Salt Lake City (Salt Lake City operator, family-owned, serving the Salt Lake Valley since 2011: recurring biweekly membership tiers — Partial Clean from $149 covering kitchen, all bathrooms, floors, and trash; Full Clean from $175 adding bedrooms, living areas, and dusting; Full Premium from $225 adding ceiling fans, vents, and deep detailing; minimum charge $149 per visit; final cost depends on square footage, bedrooms and bathrooms, how recently the home was cleaned, and pets; serves Holladay among its Salt Lake Valley cities) (queenofmaids.com); Wasatch Cleaners — House Cleaning Service in Salt Lake City (Salt Lake City operator based in South Salt Lake, 84115: one-time standard clean in normal condition from $219 for an apartment or condo / 1–2 bedrooms, $289 for a 3-bedroom family home, $345 for a 4–5 bedroom large home, priced by bedrooms and bathrooms; recurring standard visits start at $186.15 weekly, $197.10 biweekly, and $208.05 monthly; deep cleans from $319; move-in/move-out from $329; standard clean covers kitchen, bathrooms, dusting, floors, beds, and trash) (wasatch-cleaners.com); MaidThis — Maid Services in Salt Lake City (Salt Lake City operator: maid service pricing in Salt Lake City typically starts around $45–$55 per hour, or fixed rates by home size; a two-bedroom flat may cost $120–$180 per visit; costs vary with frequency, add-ons, and the condition of the home) (maidthis.com); Wolfnest — The Impact of Utah\'s Air Quality on Rental Properties: Maintenance Tips During Inversion Season (Utah source: an air inversion is a layer of warm air trapping colder air near the ground, especially common in Salt Lake City and surrounding valleys because of the bowl-like geography of the Wasatch Front; according to the Utah Department of Environmental Quality, inversion conditions occur most frequently between December and February; poor outdoor air quality leads to more dust and particulates settling indoors, building up on carpets and upholstery, ceiling fans and vents, and electronics and appliances, and excessive indoor dust can raise cleaning costs between tenants) (wolfnest.com); HomeGuide — House Cleaning Cost Guide (national figures, labeled national: a standard house cleaning costs $90 to $180 on average, and a deep cleaning costs $230 to $600; prices depend on home size and whether fridge cleaning, window cleaning, or other services are included; many services offer discounts for weekly or monthly cleanings) (homeguide.com); Thumbtack — House Cleaning in Salt Lake City, UT (national figures, labeled national: the national average cost for house cleaning ranges between $25 and $50 per hour, per cleaner; prices vary with square footage, how dirty the home is, and how often the service comes; some companies charge per square foot with a minimum) (thumbtack.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-06 via Supabase: 8 active House cleaning businesses serve the Salt Lake City metro cell — all 8 covering West Valley City ZIP 84119 (Momacia Cleaning, Roadrunner Cleaning Services, M&E Housekeeping, XKDA Professional House Keeping, Beehive House Cleaning, MaidPro Salt Lake City, Alma\'s House Cleaning, and The Cleaning Authority - Salt Lake City North), with MaidPro Salt Lake City also covering Holladay ZIP 84124; every listing in this cell has a logo on file. Featured business MaidPro Salt Lake City, House cleaning, ZIPs 84119 (West Valley City) and 84124 (Holladay), logo on file, not previously featured. The coverage grid listed 8 for this cell; the live count is 8.</div>'
