      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Salt Lake City homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Published Salt Lake prices, plus national rows labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Handyman, per hour, Salt Lake City (HomeBlue)</td><td>$40–$80</td></tr><tr><td>Handyman, per hour, Salt Lake City operator (Quality Handyman Solutions, via Thumbtack)</td><td>$65</td></tr><tr><td>Small-job minimum, same operator</td><td>$100</td></tr><tr><td>Handyman, per hour, Salt Lake City operator (We Got A Guy, via Thumbtack)</td><td>$70, plus $25 trip charge</td></tr><tr><td>Handyman, per hour, practical professional range (Built by Bradley, Salt Lake operator guide, Jan 2026)</td><td>$60–$100+</td></tr><tr><td>Published Salt Lake estimates, full span across guides (Built by Bradley)</td><td>$35–$147</td></tr><tr><td>Typical task, median (Airtasker, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$150</td></tr><tr><td>Typical task, middle half of jobs (Airtasker, Salt Lake City)</td><td>$80–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, billed by the task (Airtasker, Salt Lake City)</td><td>about $75</td></tr><tr><td>4 hours of work, Salt Lake City (HomeBlue)</td><td>$170–$320</td></tr><tr><td>8 hours of work, Salt Lake City (HomeBlue)</td><td>$340–$640</td></tr><tr><td>Self-employed / company, per hour, national (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$50–$80 / $75–$125</td></tr><tr><td>Minimum charge, national (HomeGuide via EvenQuote, national)</td><td>$75–$200</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A 30-minute fix booked alone still pays the minimum — $100 at one Salt Lake operator above, before materials. The same fix as the third item on a half-day list costs its share of $170 to $320 and nothing extra for the drive. The list is the discount in this trade.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Salt Lake City?</h3><p><strong>The guides disagree, and the gap is real money.</strong> HomeBlue puts Salt Lake at $40 to $80 an hour. A Salt Lake operator writing in January 2026 puts professional work at $60 to $100+ and notes published estimates for this city span $35 to $147 an hour, with one guide averaging $98. Ask each one what the job costs in total, not just the hourly number.</p><p><strong>Winter writes part of the list here.</strong> Airtasker’s Salt Lake page puts it straight: snowy winters and the spring thaw show up as problems around gutters, exterior trim, windows, and doors, and the freeze-thaw cycle makes gutter and ice-dam repairs a recurring job, not a one-off. In West Valley City (84120), that’s November work — seal the window and fix the trim before the cold settles in.</p><p><strong>Old plaster is slower work than drywall.</strong> The Avenues, Yalecrest, and Sugar House are full of early-1900s to 1940s homes with original trim and plaster walls. Patching that kind of wall without damaging it is a different job from patching a newer build, and Airtasker puts several plaster repairs in an older home toward the top of its range.</p><p><strong>Materials sit outside the hourly rate.</strong> HomeBlue’s Salt Lake table is labor only. Ask before the visit: is that hinge, patch compound, or trim piece in the price, or on top of it?</p><h3>What can a handyman legally do in Utah?</h3><p>Utah Code 58-55-305, effective May 7, 2025, lets a person do repair or improvement work without a contractor license when the whole job — labor, materials, and every change added later — comes to <strong>less than $7,000</strong>. Older guides still quoting a $3,000 cap are out of date.</p><p>Two limits still bite. Past <strong>$3,000</strong>, the person has to file a one-time affirmation with the state showing liability insurance, and workers compensation if they have employees. And work on a plumbing or electrical system, an HVAC system, or a gas appliance still has to be done by a licensed or certified person for that trade. A faucet swap is one thing. A new circuit is another.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get it done right</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Hand over the whole list at once.</strong> One Salt Lake operator says it in his own pricing notes: come up with a list, and it works out better for both of you. One $100 minimum spread over five small jobs beats five minimums.</li><li><strong>Pick hourly or flat on purpose.</strong> We Got A Guy charges $70 an hour plus a $25 trip charge, or a set price — the set price locks the most you’ll pay for a job that stays inside the agreed scope. For a job with a clear end, flat is usually safer.</li><li><strong>Send photos before the visit.</strong> A wide shot and a close-up tell the handyman what to bring. A return trip for one part is billable time you didn’t need to buy.</li><li><strong>Do the winter jobs in one fall visit.</strong> Gutters, trim, windows, and doors are one list in Salt Lake, not four calls spread across the cold months.</li></ul><h3>A Salt Lake City handyman business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Better Valley Handyman Services</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering handyman work at your location in West Valley City (84120). See its listing: <a href="/business/better-valley-handyman-services">Better Valley Handyman Services on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 6 handyman businesses in the Salt Lake City metro, all covering West Valley City (84120): <a href="/#/browse?zip=84120">search handyman near 84120</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/handyman/salt-lake-city/">Handyman in Salt Lake City</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Home needs cleaning too? See the Salt Lake City house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-salt-lake-city/">How much does house cleaning cost in Salt Lake City?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Denver handyman cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-a-handyman-cost-in-denver/">How much does a handyman cost in Denver?</a></p>{{img:2}}<div class="disclosure"><strong>Sources.</strong> HomeBlue — Handyman Prices in Salt Lake City, Utah (Salt Lake City hourly rate $40–$80; 1 hour $40–$80, 2 hours $90–$160, 3 hours $130–$240, 4 hours $170–$320, 5 hours $210–$400, 6 hours $260–$480, 7 hours $300–$560, 8 hours $340–$640, materials extra; price rises with emergency service, a required trade license or specialized skill, hard-to-reach location, special equipment, expensive supplies, work spanning several days, a required permit, or a dump fee; many Salt Lake projects need no permit, but an exterior door replacement sometimes does and decks of a certain height and size may) (homeblue.com); Built by Bradley — How much does a handyman cost in Salt Lake City, Utah? (Salt Lake operator guide, published January 8, 2026: roughly $60–$100+ per hour as a reasonable ballpark for general handyman labor in Salt Lake City, higher for specialized work, established companies, urgent service, or complicated projects; current 2026 local pricing guides vary — one puts the typical Salt Lake range around $35–$85/hour, another estimates roughly $49–$147/hour with a $98 average, so published Salt Lake estimates span roughly $35 to $147 per hour; quoted project prices often incorporate labor, overhead, materials, and business costs; bundling several small projects into one visit and sending wide, medium, and close-up photos before the appointment are the guide’s price advice) (builtbybradley.co); Airtasker — Find Trusted Handymen in Salt Lake City (Salt Lake City handyman tasks generally run around a median of $150, with the middle half of jobs typically falling between $80 and $250 depending on scope; jobs billed hourly rather than by the task tend to run around $75 an hour; larger jobs like a full gutter clean-out or several plaster repairs in an older home land toward the higher end, quick fixes like hanging a mirror toward the lower end; Salt Lake City’s snowy winters and spring thaw can expose minor issues around gutters, exterior trim, windows, and doors, and the freeze-thaw cycle means gutter and ice-dam repairs are a recurring need; the Avenues, 9th and 9th, and Yalecrest have original trim, window sashes, and plaster walls from early-1900s to 1940s bungalows and Craftsman-style homes, and Sugar House is known for early-1900s to 1940s Craftsman and bungalow-style homes) (airtasker.com); Thumbtack — Quality Handyman Solutions, Salt Lake City, UT (Salt Lake operator’s own pricing notes on its Thumbtack profile: general handyman work is $65 an hour; small jobs carry a $100 minimum; larger jobs are priced on a bid basis with free quotes up to a 20-mile radius from Salt Lake City; hourly billing when it is unsure how long the job will take; the operator recommends customers come up with a list of things to do, saying it works out better for both sides) (thumbtack.com); Thumbtack — We Got A Guy Handyman, Salt Lake City, UT (Salt Lake operator’s own pricing notes on its Thumbtack profile: generally a $25 trip charge and $70.00 per hour; most jobs can be charged by the hour or at a set price, and the set price locks in the maximum amount charged for a specific job that stays within its scope; the business covers home repair and improvement work including painting, carpentry, and replacing electrical devices and plumbing fixtures) (thumbtack.com); Utah Code 58-55-305 — Exemptions from licensure, effective May 7, 2025 (official Utah Legislature text: a person may engage in the alteration, repair, remodeling, or addition to or improvement of a building with a contracted or agreed value of less than $7,000, including both labor and materials and all changes or additions, without a contractor license; work in the plumbing and electrical trades on such a project, if it involves an electrical or plumbing system, shall be performed by a licensed electrical or plumbing contractor; installation, repair, or replacement of a gas appliance or combustion system must be performed by a certified person, an HVAC system by a licensed HVAC contractor, a water-based fire protection system and a radon system by licensed contractors; if the total value of the project is greater than $3,000, the person shall file a one-time affirmation with the division that they have public liability insurance and, if applicable, workers compensation insurance) (le.utah.gov); EvenQuote — Handyman Price List 2026, citing HomeGuide (national figures, labeled national: self-employed handymen $50–$80/hr and corporate $75–$125/hr; most handymen have a $75–$200 minimum and may add a $30–$80 trip charge; national job prices sourced to HomeGuide, Fixr, and Thumbtack; Salt Lake City is not one of the 33 cities in EvenQuote’s city table, so no EvenQuote city row is quoted for Salt Lake) (evenquote.com); Van Squads directory, verified live 2026-11-07 via Supabase: 6 active Handyman businesses serve the Salt Lake City metro, all covering West Valley City ZIP 84120 (As You Wish Handyman, Better Valley Handyman Services, Fast Fair Friendly Handymen, Fix It Up Handyman Services, Su Casa Handyman, and Your Handyman Pros); every listing has a logo on file. Featured business Better Valley Handyman Services, Handyman, ZIP 84120 (West Valley City), logo on file, not previously featured. The coverage grid listed 6 for this cell; the live count is 6.</div>'
